---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import SectionBadge from "../../components/SectionBadge.astro";

const updatedAt = "4 July 2026";
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="Information about personal data processing on the Telperion website."
>
  <section class="pt-12 pb-8 px-4 max-w-4xl mx-auto text-center">
    <SectionBadge> Privacy </SectionBadge>
    <h1 class="text-4xl md:text-5xl font-serif font-bold mb-6">
      Privacy <span class="italic">Policy</span>
    </h1>
    <p class="text-lg text-dark-green/80 font-medium">
      This page explains what personal data we process when you visit
      telperion.cz, contact Telperion, request a workshop or make a donation.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-4 text-sm text-dark-green/60 font-medium">
      Last updated: {updatedAt}
    </p>
  </section>

  <article class="container mx-auto px-4 pb-16 max-w-4xl">
    <div class="space-y-10 text-dark-green/85 leading-relaxed">
      <section class="border-t border-brand-green/20 pt-8">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-serif font-bold mb-4">Controller</h2>
        <p>
          The data controller is <strong>Telperion, z.s.</strong>, company ID
          21104271, registered at Uvozova 261/6, 252 62 Unetice, Czech Republic.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3">
          Contact for privacy questions and data subject requests:{" "}
          <a
            href="mailto:info@telperion.cz"
            class="font-bold text-brand-green hover:underline"
          >
            info@telperion.cz
          </a>
          .
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="border-t border-brand-green/20 pt-8">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-serif font-bold mb-4">
          What we process and why
        </h2>
        <div class="space-y-6">
          <div>
            <h3 class="text-lg font-bold mb-2">
              Website operation and security
            </h3>
            <p>
              When you visit the website, technical data needed to deliver and
              secure the page may be processed. This usually includes IP
              address, access time, requested URL, browser information and
              operational logs. The legal basis is our legitimate interest in
              operating a functional and secure website and, where applicable,
              compliance with legal obligations.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div>
            <h3 class="text-lg font-bold mb-2">Traffic and performance</h3>
            <p>
              We use Vercel Web Analytics and Vercel Speed Insights for
              aggregate traffic, error and performance measurement. According to
              Vercel documentation, Web Analytics does not use third-party
              cookies and Speed Insights is not tied to a specific visitor or IP
              address. The legal basis is our legitimate interest in improving
              and securing the website.
            </p>
            <p class="mt-3">
              We also use Sentry for technical error monitoring. If an error
              occurs on the website, Sentry may process the error message, stack
              trace, page URL, event time, browser, device, operating system,
              environment and other technical context needed to find and fix the
              issue. Sentry Session Replay is disabled in the website
              configuration, default sending of personal identifiers is
              disabled, and we do not use Sentry for marketing or profiling. The
              legal basis is our legitimate interest in keeping the website
              functional, secure and reliable.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div>
            <h3 class="text-lg font-bold mb-2">Contact form</h3>
            <p>
              If you send a workshop request or message through the form, we
              process the data you provide: name, email address, optional phone
              number, selected programme, form language and message content. The
              form is technically processed through Formspree. We use the data
              to reply, arrange a programme and continue communication. The
              legal basis is pre-contractual steps or our legitimate interest in
              handling your request.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div>
            <h3 class="text-lg font-bold mb-2">Email and phone</h3>
            <p>
              If you contact us by email or phone, we process your contact
              details and the content of the communication so we can respond and
              handle any follow-up cooperation.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div>
            <h3 class="text-lg font-bold mb-2">Donations</h3>
            <p>
              Selecting an amount and generating the payment QR code happens in
              your browser and does not by itself send us personal data. If you
              make a bank transfer, we process payment data from bank statements
              and the transparent account for accounting, donation records and
              legal compliance.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div>
            <h3 class="text-lg font-bold mb-2">Interactive map</h3>
            <p>
              The home page embeds a uMap map hosted by OpenStreetMap France.
              The map is loaded only after you click the map loading button;
              until then, we do not connect to uMap/OpenStreetMap France. The
              map provider receives technical browser data and may set a
              technical cookie needed to operate the service. If the map asks
              for geolocation, the permission is controlled by your browser;
              Telperion does not receive your location.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="border-t border-brand-green/20 pt-8">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-serif font-bold mb-4">
          Cookies and similar technologies
        </h2>
        <p>
          Telperion's own website code does not set marketing or analytics
          cookies. We do not use ad pixels, remarketing or profiling. For that
          reason, we do not currently show a cookie consent banner.
        </p>
        <ul class="mt-4 list-disc pl-6 space-y-2">
          <li>
            Vercel Web Analytics does not use third-party cookies according to
            Vercel documentation and works with aggregate statistics.
          </li>
          <li>
            uMap/OpenStreetMap France may set the technical{" "}
            <code>csrftoken</code>
            cookie after you click to load the embedded map.
          </li>
          <li>
            Sentry is configured for technical error reporting without Session
            Replay and without marketing or profiling use.
          </li>
          <li>
            The website uses <code>sessionStorage</code> to remember that you
            closed an event popup during the current session. If your browser
            already contains an older <code>zvoleny-jazyk</code> value, the form
            may read it only to prefill the inquiry language.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="border-t border-brand-green/20 pt-8">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-serif font-bold mb-4">
          Who may access the data
        </h2>
        <p>
          We disclose data only as needed to operate the website and handle
          communication. The main recipient and processor categories are Vercel
          for hosting, analytics and performance measurement, Formspree for the
          contact form, Sentry for technical error monitoring, our email
          provider, Fio banka for bank donations, uMap/OpenStreetMap France for
          the embedded map, and accounting, legal or public authorities where
          required by law or legal claims.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3">
          Some services may process data outside the EU/EEA, especially in the
          United States. In such cases, we rely on the contractual and security
          mechanisms provided by those services.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="border-t border-brand-green/20 pt-8">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-serif font-bold mb-4">Retention</h2>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2">
          <li>
            Requests and inquiries are kept for as long as needed to handle them
            and continue communication. If needed to document an agreement or
            protect legal claims, we keep them for up to 3 years from the last
            communication unless the law requires a longer period.
          </li>
          <li>
            Accounting and donation records are kept for the period required by
            accounting and tax law.
          </li>
          <li>
            Technical logs, error reports, analytics and performance data are
            retained by the service providers according to their rules and
            configuration; we use them in aggregate or operational form.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="border-t border-brand-green/20 pt-8">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-serif font-bold mb-4">Your rights</h2>
        <p>
          You may request access to your personal data, rectification, erasure,
          restriction of processing, data portability where applicable, and you
          may object to processing based on legitimate interest. Where
          processing is based on consent, you may withdraw it at any time.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3">
          You also have the right to lodge a complaint with the{" "}
          <a
            href="https://uoou.gov.cz/"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
            class="font-bold text-brand-green hover:underline"
          >
            Czech Data Protection Authority
          </a>
          .
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="border-t border-brand-green/20 pt-8">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-serif font-bold mb-4">Security</h2>
        <p>
          The website uses HTTPS, access to data is limited to people and
          services that need it, and the public website is kept separate from
          internal records. We do not intentionally process special categories
          of personal data through the website and we do not operate user
          accounts, comments, a newsletter or an e-shop.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </article>
</Layout>
